sentences.l:
and of Tros in turn three sons, blameless, were born,
Ilus and Assaracus and godlike Ganymede,
who indeed became the most beautiful of mortal men;

and the spear over his back in the earth
stood, eager, and through both circles it tore
of the man-covering shield;

but Achilles
eager rushed on, having drawn his sharp sword,
terribly crying out;

and he took a rock in his hand,
Aeneas, a great work, which not two men could carry,
such as mortals now are;

sentences.t:
ἀλλὰ τί ἢ νῦν οὗτος ἀναίτιος ἄλγεα πάσχει
μὰψ ἕνεκ’ ἀλλοτρίων ἀχέων, κεχαρισμένα δ’ αἰεὶ
δῶρα θεοῖσι δίδωσι τοὶ οὐρανὸν εὐρὺν ἔχουσιν;

sentences.tr:
alla ti ē nyn houtos anaitios algea paschei
maps henek’ allotriōn acheōn, kecharismena d’ aiei
dōra theoisi didōsi toi ouranon euryn echousin;

sentences.l:
But come, let us ourselves lead him out from under death,
lest in some way the son-of-Cronus too be angered, if Achilles
this man should kill;
